    "abstract": "Abstract A core responsibility of the Federal Reserve is to ensure financial stability by acting as the lender of last resort through its Discount Window (DW). The DW, however, has not been effective because its usage is stigmatized. In this paper, we use theory and experiments to study how such stigma can be cured. We find that behavioral inertia makes it difficult to fix a stigmatized DW, but adding a new backstop facility can help mitigate stigma. These results are consistent with the Federal Reserve’s experience. (JEL E58, G01, C92)",
    "abstract_source": "crossref_doi",
    "abstract_zh": "摘要 美联储的一项核心职责是通过贴现窗口（DW）作为最后贷款人，以维护金融稳定。然而，由于使用贴现窗口存在污名化问题，其有效性受到制约。本文通过理论与实验研究，探讨如何消除此类污名。我们发现，行为惯性使得修复污名化的贴现窗口困难重重，但增设新的后备融资工具有助于缓解污名化。这些结论与美联储的实际经验相符。（JEL E58, G01, C92）",
